      <span class="eyebrow on-dark">The gods we use</span>
    </div>
    <div class="hero-inner wrap">
      <h1 class="rv"><span class="line">Calling</span><span class="line">All <em>Gods</em></span></h1>
      <p class="hero-sub rv d1">Two paintings, each twelve and a half feet high and twenty-five feet wide, stand side by side as one unbroken wall. From across the room they look like devotion: vast, intricate, more than the eye can hold. Walk closer and the gods start to misbehave: cartoons, memes, historical figures, villains, the faces nobody admits to praying to.</p>
      <div class="hero-meta rv d2">
        <span>Venue<b>Parsons School of Design · NY</b></span>
        <span>Dates<b>December 2026 – March 2027</b></span>
        <span>Scale<b>Two paintings · 12.5 × 25 ft each</b></span>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="scrollcue" aria-hidden="true"><span>Scroll</span><span class="bar"></span></div>
  </header>

  <!-- THESIS -->
