    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="head">
        <h2 class="rv">The two<br>paintings</h2>
        <span class="kicker rv d1">One body. One survivor. Side by side.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="bento">
        <article class="pcard left rv">
          <div class="pic"><span class="plate-no">i</span><img src="./images/studio/03-guernica.jpg" alt="La Liberté de Guernica, painting by Raghava KK" loading="lazy" /></div>
          <div class="body">
            <div class="t">La Liberté de <em>Guernica</em></div>
            <p class="d">On the left, a woman standing on the ruins of Guernica. Not free, not winning, still standing. Endurance without a rescue is its own kind of dignity.</p>
            <span class="meta">Acrylic on canvas · 12.5 × 25 ft · 2022 – 2026</span>
          </div>
        </article>
        <article class="pcard right rv d1">
          <div class="pic"><span class="plate-no">ii</span><img src="./images/Vishwaroopa.jpg" alt="Vishwaroopa, painting by Raghava KK" loading="lazy" /></div>
          <div class="body">
            <div class="t"><em>Vishwaroopa</em></div>
            <p class="d">On the right, the universal form from the Bhagavad Gita. One body holding everything that cannot be held together. Gods, ideologies, time, violence, contradiction, all at once. The terror is real and not talked down.</p>
            <span class="meta">Acrylic on canvas · 12.5 × 25 ft · 2022 – 2026</span>
          </div>
        </article>
